<h2>"Pursuit - Confront the Culprit" and "Tower of Dolls - Castlevania" Mashup</h2>
<audio controls src=https://github.com/Thysbelon/midi2sseq/raw/refs/heads/gh-pages/jfa-pursuit-x-tower-of-dolls/AA2-pursuit-tower-of-dolls-trimmed-faded.flac style=width:100%></audio>
<p>I was daydreaming about a hypothetical Ace Attorney X Castlevania crossover fangame I'll probably never make, in which Athena Cykes defends Soma Kurusu in court while Franziska von Karma prosecutes, set around the year 2036; and while daydreaming I thought of this mashup.
<p>I've had my own custom software to inject edited music into NDS ROMs for about 2 years now; I worked on this software with the intention of using it to record mashups from real DS hardware, but I was unfamiliar with the process of recording a console's audio output, so I was too nervous to attempt it until I made this mashup.
<p><a href=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n07W7zOkKKs target=_blank>Tiny Town X Quartz Quadrant</a>, the first NDS mashup I made using my ROM injection software, was recorded off of the MelonDS emulator running the ROM. This mashup was recorded off of a real CTR-001 3DS running the ROM via TWiLight Menu; I recorded the audio output by plugging an audio cable into the 3DS's headphone jack, and my laptop's dual headphone-microphone jack.
<p>Phoenix Wright: Ace Attorney - Justice for All doesn't have an in-game soundtest, so to get a clean recording of my edited music, I had to use my software to also silence some of the sound effects.
<p>I submitted this mashup to SiIvaGunner, and it got uploaded as an <a href=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uzepawhlu1U target=_blank>official "SiIvaGunner Rip"</a> on <time datetime="2026-11-02">November 2, 2026</time>.
<!--<p>The fact that this mashup was recorded from an edited ROM of Justice for All, on real hardware, probably makes this one of the most accurate "rips" on SiIvaGunner. <img src=/emoji/😜.svg alt=😜>-->
